MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_001: Orchel! Perfect timing. There's something I've been\nwanting to ask you.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_002: Me too! But you go first.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_003: Ever since I heard that you served in Credna's\ntemple, I've had something on my mind.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_004: You see, Aurora often talks about her Uncle Credna.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_005: Uh-oh. What does she say?
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_006: I understand he likes to talk about his travels and the\npeople he's met on the frontier.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_007: Yes, that's quite true. Credna often graces us with\nstories of his journeys.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_008: He's the kind of person who makes you think he's\na homebody then disappears for weeks.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_009: I hope he didn't...say anything to offend Aurora.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_010: No, no, it's nothing like that. I've heard he's very\nkind. Is that true?
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_011: It is, but he can also be oblivious to a degree you\nwouldn't believe.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_012: He might walk around with his clothes soaked in oil,\nmaking a mess of the temple that we have to clean.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_013: Sometimes we find him sprawled near some water,\nas if he passed out while trying to bathe.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_014: Honestly, I can't let him out of my sight. Every day,\nit's something new!
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_015: Gods and goddesses in their temples, right? I think\nthey get a little too comfortable at home sometimes.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_016: You should see how sulky Aurora gets when I beat\nher at board games.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_017: Oh my. That must be a real strain on you.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_018: Yes and no. I've been taking care of her for my\nentire temple career.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_019: So when she shows her true colors, I'm actually\nquite tickled.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_020: I know just what you mean! You think, "come on,\nenough!" but at the same time, you care so much.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_021: Haha! The secret lives of caretakers of the gods, eh?
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_022: We should do this more often, Ultand.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_023: I always wanted to make friends with a priest from\nanother temple.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_024: Friends? Is that really OK? I'm pretty sure you\noutrank me as a priest, Orchel.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_025: Does the difference in rank bother you? Then think\nof it this way...we both do the same work.
MID_SE_Orh_Hur_C_026: Hmhm. I suppose we do have a lot of common\nground. So, yeah, let's chat again sometime!
